  "story": {
    "day": 102,
    "title": "Kaya's Busy Weekend",
    "sentences": [
      "Last weekend, Kaya, a junior high school student, went to a central market.",
      "Fourteen years old, she needed to write a list for her home's order.",
      "She found a radish for fifty yen, a great deal on sale.",
      "She also bought delicious chocolate and candy from Hong Kong.",
      "A man asked, \"Pardon me, where is the fourth aisle?\"",
      "Kaya saw a police officer and an office worker nearby; she picked up litter.",
      "She cannot ski, but hoped to pass her basketball test to be captain.",
      "She admired a beautiful musical instrument, a trumpet, and looked at a movie theater poster.",
      "She bought iced tea and a Hindu cookbook. Our club members wanted it.",
      "In the afternoon, she passed a pool. She listened to which song was playing.",
      "After her bath, she ate soup. She felt ready, it was almost nine.",
      "\"Are you sure?\" an interviewer asked. \"Okay.\"",
      "\"Have we anything else for their eighty-yen snack by the fifteenth?\""
    ]
  }
}